<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  `direct` flavor manifest — merged only into the sideloaded build.

  Everything here is something Google Play would take issue with, so it lives in this
  source set and can never leak into the `play` AAB.

  1. REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES lets UpdatePlugin hand a downloaded APK to the system
     installer. That is the whole point of the direct build and is flatly prohibited
     for anything distributed through Google Play (Device and Network Abuse policy).

  2. ReminderCarAppService is the Android Auto car screen. A templated car app must
     declare one of Auto's approved categories, and a reminder app is none of them
     (navigation / parking / charging / POI / IOT / settings / messaging / calling /
     weather), so shipping it in the Play build would put every release at risk of an
     Auto review rejection for the sake of a screen. SETTINGS is the closest fit of a
     bad set and is what the sideloaded build declares. See docs/alarm-architecture.md
     and store/play-readiness.md.

  3. **The Android Auto notification declaration**, which is the part this file used to
     say was safe to ship in both flavors. `com.google.android.gms.car.application` sat
     in src/main on the reasoning that mirroring nags into the car "needs no category".
     It needs no *category*, but it does opt the app into Play's **Auto App Quality
     Guidelines as a messaging app**: the only thing `<uses name="notification"/>` means
     to Auto is "this app sends and receives messages". Play's review then tests exactly
     that and finds — correctly — that a reminder app can neither send an outgoing
     message nor receive an incoming one, which is the 2026-08-17 policy notice. No
     version of Persistent passes a messaging test, so the declaration joins the rest of
     the Auto integration in the sideloaded build. That leaves the Play build with no
     Android Auto surface at all, which is the alternative Play's own "how to fix"
     offers. `res/xml/automotive_app_desc.xml` moves with it (setup-android.mjs copies it
     into this flavor's res/, not src/main's) — a resource the entry points at is part
     of the same declaration.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES" />

    <application>
        <!-- Car API level 1 is all the list/message templates this app uses need, so it
             stays compatible with the widest set of head units. -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="androidx.car.app.minCarApiLevel"
            android:value="1" />

        <!-- Extends this build's notifications to Android Auto; points at
             res/xml/automotive_app_desc.xml (<uses name="notification"/>). Direct-only —
             see note 3 above. -->
        <meta-data
            android:name="com.google.android.gms.car.application"
            android:resource="@xml/automotive_app_desc" />

        <service
            android:name="ca.persistent.app.alarm.ReminderCarAppService"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="androidx.car.app.CarAppService" />
                <category android:name="androidx.car.app.category.SETTINGS" />
            </intent-filter>
        </service>
    </application>
</manifest>
